    "id": "prop:identified-scodite",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Under consistency and conditional exchangeability, \\(\\Psi(P)=E_P[K_X\\otimes\\{L_{Y(1)}-L_{Y(0)}\\}]\\). On the two-outcome submodel supported on \\(\\{y_-,y_+\\}\\), this becomes \\(\\Psi(P)=E_P[K_X\\otimes b_Y\\{P(Y=y_+\\mid A=1,X)-P(Y=y_+\\mid A=0,X)\\}]\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "Psi",
      "P",
      "K",
      "X",
      "L",
      "Yone",
      "Yzero",
      "Y",
      "A",
      "yminus",
      "yplus",
      "bY",
      "H"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:consistency",
      "ass:exchangeability",
      "ass:outcome-kernel-characteristic",
      "def:model-class"
    ],
    "justification": "This fixes the law-valued causal target while supplying a legal two-outcome reduction for the lower-bound construction.",
    "gap": "Jain and Luedtke give the general identifying moment; the embedded two-outcome reduction is needed here to audit exact-null mixtures and source membership without shrinking the ambient model to CATE.",
    "consumer": "The reduction makes the least-favorable experiment computable while the resulting frontier continues to govern general conditional outcome laws.",
    "proof_tex": "For \\(a\\in\\{0,1\\}\\), consistency gives \\(L_Y=L_{Y(a)}\\) on \\(\\{A=a\\}\\). Conditional exchangeability and iterated expectation give, for \\(P_X\\)-almost every \\(x\\),\n\\[\n\\nu_a(x)=E_P[L_Y\\mid A=a,X=x]=E_P[L_{Y(a)}\\mid X=x].\n\\]\nThe sections are Bochner integrable by boundedness of the outcome kernel. Hence\n\\[\n\\Psi(P)=E_P[K_X\\otimes\\{\\nu_1(X)-\\nu_0(X)\\}]\n=E_P[K_X\\otimes\\{L_{Y(1)}-L_{Y(0)}\\}].\n\\]\nOn the two-outcome submodel, with \\(m_a(x)=P(Y=y_+\\mid A=a,X=x)\\),\n\\[\n\\nu_a(x)=m_a(x)L_{y_+}+\\{1-m_a(x)\\}L_{y_-}\n=L_{y_-}+m_a(x)b_Y.\n\\]\nThus \\(U(x)=\\{m_1(x)-m_0(x)\\}b_Y\\), and substitution proves the second formula.",
